						long: "The Semi-Square (45 degrees) is half of a square, carrying a similar but less intense quality of tension. It represents internal agitation, minor frustrations, and the kind of low-grade irritation that eventually forces adjustments. Unlike the square, which demands immediate confrontation, the semi-square builds pressure gradually. It often manifests as restlessness, impatience, or dissatisfaction with the status quo. When consciously worked with, this aspect motivates incremental changes that prevent larger crises from developing.",
