				name: "Daridra Yoga",
				description: "The lord of the 11th house occupies the 6th, the 8th or the 12th.",
				result: "Daridra Yoga is a poverty combination and the classical description of it is unsparing: debts that accumulate, work that stays menial, and standing that erodes along with the finances. Read it as sustained pressure on the flow of gains rather than as a sentence. The 11th house governs income and increase, so placing its lord where results are spent, obstructed or lost tends to mean money leaves faster than it arrives and effort converts poorly into savings. The same source names ear complaints and strained relations with siblings beside the financial reading. No single combination settles a chart. Supporting wealth yogas, a well placed 2nd and 11th lord and favourable periods all temper this one, so the sound reading is of a weakness to manage rather than an outcome to accept.",
