				result: "Lakshmi Yoga is named for the goddess of fortune and the classical result reads accordingly: wealth in abundance, standing close to that of a ruler, a lasting name, and the conduct that earns it. Fortune here is fortune with a foundation. The 9th house carries merit, patronage and the good that arrives unearned, so a dignified and well placed 9th lord tends to make that support structural rather than occasional, with family, teachers, institutions and circumstance moving in the same direction. The strong Lagna lord is the second half of the combination, and it is what turns that support into a life the native can hold rather than one that passes through. Read the scale of it from the strength of the two lords involved, not from the presence of the combination alone.",
